  "title": "CMake: Find the liblzma.dll from minizip-ng on Windows",
  "description": "minizip-ng from vcpkg depends on bzip2, zstd, zlib (*not* zlib-ng),\nand liblzma dlls. We've only been installing the first two from\nthis CMake Find module, because vcpkg-export (the glib, libxml2,\nand zlib bundle) installed the latter two. However, as of vcpkg tag\n2025.04.09, libxml2 not longer depends on liblzma (reflecting upstream.)\n\nSo look for and copy the one that minizip-ng uses.\n\nFollowup to ba0d702a3f7355095b51c8642707a012096b35ab\n\nA subsequent commit will update the minizip-ng package (which will\nalso update its version of liblzma, ping #20569, #20013.)",
